    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d16">

                <pb facs="0027" n="15" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg15"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.24/281</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the British
                        Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lothian</hi>)</head>
                <p>The Acting Secretary of State presents his compliments to His Excellency the
                    British Ambassador and has the honor to acknowledge the receipt of Lord
                    Lothian’s note of July 13, 1940,<anchor n="23" xml:id="d16-f1"/> with further
                    reference to the dissolution of the Anglo-French Purchasing Board in the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>Lord Lothian may rest assured that this Government will continue to extend to Mr.
                    Arthur B. Purvis, in his new capacity as Director-General of the British
                    Purchasing Commission, the same facilities which were extended to him as
                    Chairman of the Anglo-French Purchasing Board.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1940-07-23">July 23,
                            1940</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
